 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R4 (block 252000) -- the SUPPLY NETWORK. Producers buy their inputs UP-CHAIN from suppliers along a sparse `supplied_by` graph (baker<-farmer grain, fishmonger<-fisherman fish, fisherman<-baitseller bait). `be_restock` buys an input for CASH -> the supplier keeper is PAID; `be_restock_credit` (keeper short of coin, supplier extends credit) mints an `Owe` ALONG the supplies edge. A FAILURE propagates the graph as the native O(edges) flood, sparse => linear: a fishmonger with no coin can't pay the fisherman -> the fisherman goes UNPAID (coin flat) -> can't buy bait up-chain next cycle -> his fish output FALLS -> HIS customers get less; nothing scripted -- it flows the edges. SEVER `supplied_by` and the up-chain owe is never minted -> the creditor is never defaulted-upon -> no affect flip / no shortfall appears (propagation is edge-mediated). `be_repay` (control) settles an owe before term. Composes existing Terms; zero new Rust.",
